prompt='''Edit image1 only, fixed64x64native case/wrist/belt crop enlarged12x, original framing/transparency unchanged. Image2 is the ACTUAL ORIGINAL SAME WALK POSE at IDENTICAL scale/registration: it establishes belt-device location. Image3 is original detailed West master device identity, NOT an exposure/color guide. Correct the incorrect LOWER three-yellow-bar meter in image1: it has been moved down below glove and redesigned. Remove that LOWER relocated copy, restoring graphite hip/belt cloth beneath it. There must be only ONE belt meter, fixed at image2 original higher belt attachment near world x128,y134..145 (crop x24,y22..33). Master design is ONE square amber/yellow SCREEN at top and FOUR SMALL ROUND amber buttons in a2x2grid below, narrow graphite housing with dull silver edging; NOT three bars. Put original meter behind the carrying wrist/glove at this same higher location. The carrying glove must naturally occlude much of it; do NOT move meter down or sideways to make entire device visible. A small original-position screen/edge peeking beside/above glove is valid if naturally visible; do not invent a second screen. Keep current case panel/size/height, both gloves and cuff connected with natural overlap, no black cavity, no transparent hole, no body clipping. Preserve belt wrench/holster on right exactly where it is, no wrench in hand. Preserve matte target graphite/ochre grade; do not copy detailed master's shiny metal/exposure or green background. Keep all other torso/hips/gear/case pixels/design stable. Return only original full square crop with correct master meter fixed higher on belt behind hand and WRONG relocated lower bar-meter gone.'''
